If we assume that throwing each item up or down stairs requires one
turn, it seems that this method would be only slightly better than
ferrying things up or down stairs one by one.  It wouldn't afford any
advantage in that respect.

It also seems that there should be a few more restrictions placed on
this, though, just for the sake of realism.  For example, a person
throwing something upstairs should have a chance of missing and either
catching the item or dropping it on the floor.  Certain items, like
crystal balls, mirrors, and potions should also have a chance of
breaking when they hit the floor.  Others, like iron balls (chained to
you) and loadstones, should not be throwable at all.

